- Shipped project: OpenAI-compatible client, base URL and model ids from env, **defaults to
  Token Factory**. README, spend table and video come from Token Factory runs.
- Development until the promo credits arrive: OpenCode Zen lists `nemotron-3-super-free`,
  `nemotron-3-ultra-free`, `nemotron-3.5-lightning-free` and `nemotron-3.5-super-vl-free` at $0
  on `https://opencode.ai/inference/openai/v1` (the Go plan is a separate base URL,
  `https://opencode.ai/inference/go/openai/v1`; check whether the Go key can hit the free ids).
  Same weights, so prompt tuning transfers. Qwen 3.7/3.8 on Go is the fallback for harness work only.
- Rule unchanged: no non-Nebius provider in docs, demo or defaults; `.redsun/` stays ignored.

## Budget (Token Factory prices, demo-scale hunt)

| Stage | Volume | Approx |
|---|---|---|
| Lightning generation | 10k programs, ~1.5k tokens out each | ~$4 |
| Ultra judge | ~300 disputed cases | ~$2 |
| Minimize, report | ~200 findings | ~$1 |

$50 of credit covers it several times over. Wall-clock is the constraint.

## Demo script (under 3 minutes)

1. 0:00 A "safe" fix on a 6-line program; run before, run after, different output. (10 s)
2. 0:15 Pick Biome 2.5.14 + three rules, start a hunt: Lightning programs streaming, sandbox
   branches fanning out, oracle hits landing in the feed.
3. 1:00 It rediscovers two known bugs; minimized repro next to the real upstream issue.
4. 1:30 Same hunt on current Biome and ruff: one new finding, Tavily dedup result, drafted issue.
5. 2:20 clang-tidy backend in 15 s (author's LLVM fix-it ground truth).
6. 2:35 Routing table and spend, all on Token Factory; one line on Sandboxes.

