ESLint backend → PR-triggered mode → Sandboxes (keep Docker) → minimize (ship un-minimized
repros) → clang-tidy backend (keep Biome + ruff). Never cut: oracles O2/O3, the dashboard,
the ground-truth rediscovery.

## What past Devpost winners looked like (survey 2026-10-17)

Galleries checked: AWS x NVIDIA Agentic AI Unleashed (2025), Dell x NVIDIA HackAI (2024),
HP x NVIDIA Developer Challenge (2025), OpenAI Open Model Hackathon (2025), ArangoDB x NVIDIA
(2025), Emergence x Nebius Enterprise Agents (2026).

- Winners are complete products with a thesis, not demos of a model: TrustSQL ("the query
  executed, the insight didn't"; verifies SQL against intent with live validation queries),
  Codence (validates PRs against meeting decisions), xShield (repo security scan with CI
  integration), Delivery Tracker, Skyrchitect.
- A verification or trust angle recurs among winners; pure generation rarely wins.
- Sponsor tech sits inside the reasoning loop and the write-up says exactly where.
- Dev-tool winners shipped an integration surface (GitHub Action, webhook, API), not just a UI.
- Write-ups follow Inspiration / What it does / How we built it / Challenges, with an
  architecture diagram and a stack table.

Applied here: lead with the "safe fix that wasn't" story, ship the dashboard plus a CLI and a
GitHub Action stub, show evidence on screen, and put Nemotron in the loop where a human would read
rule source and write adversarial programs.

## Status against this plan (2026-10-22)

Done: Biome, ruff and clang-tidy backends; oracles O1–O5; analyze and generate (Super) with a feedback
round; Token Factory Sandboxes as the execution backend (disposable VM per run, stdin tarball, parallel
evaluation); ddmin minimization with a Lightning proposal and sandbox confirmation; docs-aware Ultra judge
measured against 89 hand labels (87% accuracy, 86% precision on "real"); GitHub + Tavily dedup with Ultra
triage; evidence sheets; rule catalogs and sweeps (215 rules, ~130 findings); dashboard (ranked findings,
side-by-side evidence, live hunt feed, live re-run in a sandbox, static export); spend logging for models
and sandboxes; platform feedback notes (`docs/feedback.md`); winners survey (`docs/winners-survey-2026-10-22.md`).
Results: ruff #29452 filed; four new candidates; nine known bugs rediscovered. Credits: two $25 promo
codes applied on 2026-10-22.

Not done, by choice: ESLint backend (cut list), PR-triggered mode, SQLite store (results.json is enough).
Remaining for submission: UI redesign (last), hosting (last; static export is the fallback), demo video,
Devpost text, final sweep on current releases.

